### Toolchain pairing flow by role (REST Client). Pick the "local" environment, then run top to bottom.
### Needs studentUid, studentPassword, teacherUid, teacherPassword in rest-client.environmentVariables (.vscode/settings.json, not committed).
### Each request reads the previous responses, e.g. {{startSession.response.body.$.pairingCode}}.
### Run step 0 only before the first login; REST Client remembers cookies.

### 0. No login: expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{"stationId": "terminal-town-gate"}

### 1. Student logs in
# @name loginStudent
POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{"uid": "{{studentUid}}", "password": "{{studentPassword}}"}

### 2. Student starts a session: expect 200 with sessionId and pairingCode
# @name startSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{"stationId": "terminal-town-gate"}

### 3. Agent pairs with that code (no login needed): expect 200 with agentToken
# @name pairAgent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/pair
Content-Type: application/json

{"pairingCode": "{{startSession.response.body.$.pairingCode}}"}

### 4. The same code again: expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/pair
Content-Type: application/json

{"pairingCode": "{{startSession.response.body.$.pairingCode}}"}

### 5. Student asks for a station check: expect 200, status CHECKING
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}/check
Content-Type: application/json

{"stationId": "terminal-town-gate"}

### 6. Agent polls with its token: expect 200 and the station
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}/next
Authorization: Bearer {{pairAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}

### 7. Garbage token: expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}/next
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### 8. Failing evidence: expect 200, status FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{pairAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"os": "linux", "stationId": "terminal-town-gate", "checks": [
  {"id": "working-folder", "exitCode": 0, "output": "/home/test"},
  {"id": "pages-clone", "exitCode": 1, "output": "pages folder not found"}]}

### 9. Passing evidence: expect 200, status VERIFIED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{pairAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"os": "linux", "stationId": "terminal-town-gate", "checks": [
  {"id": "working-folder", "exitCode": 0, "output": "/home/test"},
  {"id": "pages-clone", "exitCode": 0, "output": "/home/test/opencs/pages"}]}

### 10. Student reads the final status: expect VERIFIED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}

### 11. Teacher logs in (replaces the student cookie)
# @name loginTeacher
POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{"uid": "{{teacherUid}}", "password": "{{teacherPassword}}"}

### 12. Teacher reads the student's session: expect 404 (only the owner may)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{startSession.response.body.$.sessionId}}
